Solve, algebraically, over the interval \([0,2 \pi]\).
\[
2 \sin ^{2} x+5 \cos x+1=0
\]

Solution
\[
\begin{array}{r}
2\left(1-\cos ^{2} x\right)+5 \cos x+1=0 \\
2-2 \cos ^{2} x+5 \cos x+1=0 \\
-2 \cos ^{2} x+5 \cos x+3=0 \\
2 \cos ^{2} x-5 \cos x-3=0 \\
(2 \cos x+1)(\cos x-3)=0 \\
\cos x=-\frac{1}{2} \quad \cos x=3 \\
x=\frac{2 \pi}{3}, \frac{4 \pi}{3} \quad \text { no solution }
\end{array}
\]

1 mark for substitution of an appropriate identity

1 mark for solving for \(\cos x\)

2 marks for solving for \(x\) ( \(\frac{1}{2}\) mark for each value; 1 mark for indicating no solution)

