1 mark

Solve, algebraically.
\[
\left(\frac{1}{6}\right)^{3 x+2}=6^{2 x}
\]

\section*{Solution}
\[
\begin{aligned}
\left(6^{-1}\right)^{3 x+2} & =6^{2 x} \\
6^{-3 x-2} & =6^{2 x} \\
-3 x-2 & =2 x \\
-5 x & =2 \\
x & =-\frac{2}{5}
\end{aligned}
\]

